ranked by how strong a signal their whole compound set gives for a disease
-- answering "which extract has the best effect?" rather than "which
compound".

Any \verb{(condition, disease)} pair not yet in \code{patliRResults(proj, "network_proximity")} is computed first with \code{\link[=network_proximity]{network_proximity()}}, using
\code{...}. Already-computed pairs are reused as-is (no recomputation), so
calling this repeatedly while conditions are added one at a time is cheap.
